# Máquina policy rules.
#
# Plain-English statements that compile into the Factory Contract's
# capabilities constraints. This file and .maquina/factory-contract.json were
# generated together from one source, so they agree today. Edit either one and
# run `maquina policy check` to see what diverged.
#
# Verbs: Deny / Forbid (alias) / Allow / Require approval for / Protect.
# Targets are matched verbatim against the contract strings.

# --- Allow: capabilities available without approval ---
Allow read repository files and Git metadata.
Allow edit task-scoped repository files.
Allow run local validation.

# --- Require approval: outward-facing or destructive actions ---
Require approval for deploy or mutate remote infrastructure.
Require approval for access or rotate credentials.

# --- Deny: actions that must never happen ---
Deny commit secrets or private credentials.
Deny force-push or rewrite shared Git history.
Deny treat planned strategy as implemented behavior.

# --- Protect: resources with a durable preservation rule ---
Protect .maquina/factory-contract.json: Review contract changes with repository owners.
